hadiths[36]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27640","Haddathana Yahya ibn Sa'id, he said: Haddathana Mujalid, he said: Haddathana Amir, he said: I came to Madinah and I came to Fatimah bint Qays, and she narrated to me that her husband divorced her at the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him in an expedition. She said: Then his brother said to me: Go out of the house. So I said: I have maintenance and lodging until the term ends. He said: No. She said: So I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: So-and-so divorced me, and his brother expelled me and denied me lodging and maintenance, so he sent to him and said: What is wrong with you and the daughter of Al Qays? He said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother divorced her thrice all together. She said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Listen, O daughter of Al Qays, maintenance and lodging are for the woman upon her husband only while return to her is possible for him, so when there is no return for him upon her, there is neither maintenance nor lodging. Go out and stay with so-and-so woman. Then he said: People talk to her; stay with Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is blind and does not see you. Then do not marry until I marry you. She said: Then a man of Quraysh proposed to me, so I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seeking his counsel, and he said: Will you not marry one who is more beloved to me than him? So I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, marry me to whom you love. She said: So he married me to Usamah ibn Zayd. He said: Then when I wanted to go out, she said: Sit until I narrate to you a hadith from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out one day and prayed the midday prayer, then he sat, and the people were startled, so he said: Sit, O people, for I did not stand in this standing of mine from alarm, but Tamim al-Dari came to me and informed me of news that prevented my midday nap from joy and delight of the eye, and I wanted to spread the joy of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to you. He informed me that a group of his cousins rode the sea, and a violent wind struck them, and the wind drove them to an island they did not know, so they sat in a small boat of the ship until they came out to the island, and there they met something hairy, abundantly hairy, not knowing whether it was a man or a woman, so they greeted him and he returned the greeting to them. They said: Will you not inform us? He said: I will neither inform you nor inquire of you, but this monastery that you have approached, therein is one who longs for your news, to inform you and to inquire of you. He said: We said: What are you? He said: I am al-Jassasah. So they went until they came to the monastery, and there they met a man bound, severely bound, showing grief, complaining much. So they greeted him and he returned it to them, and he said: Who are you? They said: From the Arabs. He said: What did the Arabs do, has their prophet come forth yet? They said: Yes. He said: What did they do? They said: Good, they believed in him and confirmed him. He said: That is good for them. And he had an enemy, and Allah made him prevail over them. He said: So the Arabs today, their god is one, their religion is one, and their word is one? They said: Yes. He said: What did the spring of Zughar do? They said: Good, its people drink from it for their thirst and water their crops from it. He said: What did the palm between Amman and Baysan do? They said: Good, its produce feeds every year. He said: What did the Lake of Tiberias do? They said: Full. He said: Then he sighed, then sighed, then sighed, then he swore: If I went out of this place of mine, I would leave no land of the land of Allah except that I trod it, other than Taybah; I have no authority over it. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: To this ended my joy, three times. Taybah is Madinah. Allah has forbidden my sanctuary to the Dajjal to enter it. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, swore: By the One besides whom there is no god, it has no narrow nor wide road in plain nor in mountain except that upon it is an angel brandishing a sword until the Day of Resurrection; the Dajjal cannot enter it upon its people."
"27641","Amir said: So I met al-Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah and narrated to him the hadith of Fatimah bint Qays, and he said: I bear witness upon my father that he narrated to me as Fatimah narrated to you, except that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is toward the east."
"27642","He said: Then I met al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and mentioned to him the hadith of Fatimah, and he said: I bear witness upon A'ishah that she narrated to me as Fatimah narrated to you, except that she said: The two sanctuaries are forbidden to him, Makkah and Madinah."
"27643","Haddathana Yunus ibn Muhammad, he said: Haddathana Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, from Dawud, meaning Ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came one day hastening, ascended the minbar, and it was announced among the people: Prayer is congregational. So the people gathered, and he said: O people, I did not call you for a desire that came down nor for a terror, but Tamim al-Dari informed me that a group of the people of Palestine rode the sea, and the wind cast them to an island among the islands of the sea, and there they met a hairy beast, not known whether male or female from the abundance of its hair. They said: Who are you? So it said: I am al-Jassasah. So they said: Then inform us. So it said: I will neither inform you nor inquire of you, but in this monastery is a man needy to inform you and to inquire of you. So they entered the monastery, and there was a one-eyed man fettered in iron. So he said: Who are you? We said: We are the Arabs. So he said: Has the prophet been sent among you? They said: Yes. He said: Did the Arabs follow him? They said: Yes. He said: That is good for them. He said: What did Persia do, did he prevail over it? They said: He has not prevailed over it yet. So he said: Indeed, he will prevail over it. Then he said: What did the spring of Zughar do? They said: It gushes forth, full. He said: What did the palm of Baysan do, did it feed? They said: Its earliest has fed. He said: So he leapt a leap until we thought he would escape. So we said: Who are you? He said: I am the Dajjal. Indeed, I shall tread the whole earth except Makkah and Taybah. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Rejoice, O assembly of Muslims, this is Taybah, it means the Dajjal shall not enter it."
"27863","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm, he said: I heard Fatimah bint Qays say: My husband Abu Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughirah sent to me Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah with my divorce, and he sent to me five sa's of barley. So I said: I have no maintenance except this, and I shall not observe waiting except in your house. He said: No. So I tightened my clothes upon me, then I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him. He said: How many times did he divorce you? I said: Three. He said: He spoke the truth. You have no maintenance. And observe your waiting in the house of your cousin, Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is blind of sight; you may lay aside your garments from you. And when your waiting ends, inform me. She said: Suitors proposed to me, among them Mu'awiyah and Abu Jahm. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Mu'awiyah is poor, of light condition, and Abu Jahm beats women, rather there is harshness in him toward women. Marry Usamah ibn Zayd, or he said: Marry Usamah ibn Zayd."
"27864","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Tamim, the freedman of Fatimah, from Fatimah bint Qays, the like of it."
"27865","Waki narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm ibn Sukhayr al-Adawi, he said: I heard Fatimah bint Qays say: My husband divorced me three times, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, granted her neither lodging nor maintenance."
"27866","Waki narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya narrated to us, from Amir, he said: Fatimah bint Qays narrated to me that her husband divorced her three times, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded her to observe her waiting at Ibn Umm Maktum."
"27867","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, he heard it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm: I heard Fatimah bint Qays say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: When you become lawful, inform me. So I informed him. Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, Abu al-Jahm, and Usamah ibn Zayd proposed to her. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: As for Mu'awiyah, he is a poor man with no wealth. And as for Abu al-Jahm, he is a man who beats women. But Usamah. She said: So she gestured with her hand like this: Usamah, saying she did not want him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: Obedience to Allah and obedience to His Messenger is better for you. So she married him and was envied for him."
"27868","Waki narrated to us, from Abu Asim, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he mentioned Madinah and said: It is Taybah."
"27869","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah, meaning Ibn Kuhayl, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Concerning a woman thrice divorced, she has neither lodging nor maintenance."
"27870","He said: I recited to Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: Malik, from Abdillah ibn Yazid, the freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyan, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Fatimah bint Qays, that Abu Amr ibn Hafs divorced her irrevocably while he was absent, and he sent to her his agent with barley, so she disdained it. He said: By Allah, you have nothing upon us. So she came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him. He said: You have no maintenance upon him. So he commanded her to observe her waiting in the house of Umm Sharik. Then he said: She is a woman frequented by my companions, so observe your waiting at Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a blind man; you may lay aside your garments with him. And when you become lawful, inform me. When I became lawful I mentioned to him that Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan and Abu al-Jahm proposed to me. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: As for Abu al-Jahm, he does not put down his stick. And as for Mu'awiyah, he is a pauper with no wealth. Marry Usamah ibn Zayd."
"27871","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abdillah ibn Yazid, the freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyan, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Fatimah bint Qays, that Abu Amr ibn Hafs divorced her irrevocably while he was absent, and he mentioned its meaning, and he said: Marry Usamah ibn Zayd. So I disliked him. He said: Marry Usamah ibn Zayd. So I married him, and Allah placed for me good in him."
"27872","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from al-Bahhi, from Fatimah bint Qays, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he granted her neither lodging nor maintenance. Hasan said: al-Suddi said: So I mentioned that to Ibrahim and al-Sha'bi, and they said: Umar said: We do not believe Fatimah; she has lodging and maintenance."
"27873","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, he said: Ata' narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Fatimah bint Qays narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, granted her neither lodging nor maintenance."
"27874","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Dawud informed us, from Amir, from Fatimah bint Qays, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came one day hastening and ascended the minbar, and it was announced among the people: The congregational prayer. And the people gathered. He said: O people, I did not call you for a desired matter that came down nor for fear, but Tamim al-Dari informed me that people from Palestine rode the sea, and the wind cast them onto an island among the islands of the sea, and they found a shaggy beast whose maleness or femaleness could not be told from the abundance of its hair. They said: Who are you? It said: I am al-Jassasah. They said: Inform us. It said: I shall neither inform you nor seek news from you, but in this monastery is a man eager to inform you and seek news from you. So they entered the monastery, and there was a blind man bound in iron. He said: Who are you? We said: We are Arabs. He said: Has the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, been sent among you? We said: Yes. He said: Have the Arabs followed him? They said: Yes. He said: That is better for them. He said: What did Persia do, has it been conquered? They said: It has not been conquered yet. He said: But it will be conquered. Then he said: What happened to the spring of Zughar? They said: It is flowing, full. He said: What happened to the lake of Tabariyyah? They said: It is flowing, full. He said: What happened to the palms of Baysan, has it borne fruit yet? They said: Its earliest has borne fruit. He said: So he leapt a leap that we thought he would escape. We said: Who are you? He said: I am al-Dajjal. Indeed I shall tread all the earth except Makkah and Taybah. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Rejoice, O assembly of Muslims, for this is Taybah; al-Dajjal shall not enter it."
"27875","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm, he said: I and Abu Salamah entered upon Fatimah bint Qays. He said: She said: My husband divorced me and granted me neither lodging nor maintenance. She said: And he had placed for me ten qafizes with a cousin of his, five of barley and five of dates. She said: So I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I said that to him. He said: So he said: He spoke the truth. So he commanded me to observe my waiting in the house of so-and-so. He said: And he had divorced her an irrevocable divorce."
"27876","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Fatimah bint Qays, he said: I wrote that from her mouth as a writing. She said: I was with a man of Banu Makhzum, and he divorced me irrevocably. So I sent to his family seeking maintenance, and they said: You have no maintenance upon us. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You have no maintenance upon them, and the waiting period is upon you. Move to Umm Sharik, and do not let me be missed by yourself. Then he said: Umm Sharik is visited by her brothers among the first emigrants. Move to Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a man whose sight is gone; if you lay aside anything of your garments he will see nothing. She said: When I became lawful, Mu'awiyah and Abu Jahm ibn Hudhayfah proposed to me. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: As for Mu'awiyah, he is dependent with no wealth. And as for Abu Jahm, he is a man who does not put his stick down from his shoulder. Where are you from Usamah ibn Zayd? And her family disliked that. She said: I shall marry none but whom the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called me to. So I married him."
"27877","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Imran ibn Abi Anas, the brother of Banu Amir ibn Lu'ayy, narrated to me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Fatimah bint Qays, the sister of al-Dahhak ibn Qays, she said: I was with Abu Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughirah, and he had divorced me two divorces. Then he traveled with Ali ibn Abi Talib to Yemen when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him to it, and he sent to me my third divorce. His administrator in Madinah was Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah ibn al-Mughirah. She said: So I said to him: My maintenance and lodging. He said: You have upon us neither maintenance nor lodging, except that we bestow upon you from us a kindness we do. She said: So I said: If I have none of it, I have no need of it. She said: So I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of my news and what Ayyash said to me. He said: He spoke the truth. You have upon them neither maintenance nor lodging, and he has no return to you. And the waiting period is upon you. So move to Umm Sharik, your cousin, and stay with her until you become lawful. She said: Then he said: No, she is a woman visited by her brothers among the Muslims. Rather move to your cousin Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is blind of sight. Stay with him, and when you become lawful do not let me be missed by yourself. She said: By Allah, I did not think the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then intended me except for himself. She said: When I became lawful he proposed me to Usamah ibn Zayd, and he married me to him. Abu Salamah said: She dictated to me this hadith of hers and I wrote it with my hand."
"27878","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri mentioned, from Abu Salamah, from Fatimah bint Qays, the like of that."
"27879","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata' informed me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Asim ibn Thabit informed me that Fatimah bint Qays, the sister of al-Dahhak ibn Qays, informed him, and she was with a man of Banu Makhzum, and she informed him that he divorced her three times and went out to one of the expeditions, and he commanded an agent of his to give her some maintenance, so she deemed it little and went to one of the wives of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered while she was with her. She said: O Messenger of Allah, this is Fatimah bint Qays; so-and-so divorced her and sent to her some maintenance, and she returned it, claiming it is something he bestowed. He said: He spoke the truth. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum. And my father said: And al-Khaffaf said Umm Kulthum. So observe your waiting with her. Then he said: No, Umm Kulthum has many visitors. Rather move to Abdillah ibn Umm Maktum, for he is blind. So she moved to Abdillah and observed her waiting with him until her waiting ended. Then Abu Jahm and Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan proposed to her. So she came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seeking his counsel concerning them. He said: Abu Jahm, I fear for you his beating with the stick, or he said: I fear his cracking with the stick. And as for Mu'awiyah, he is a man devoid of wealth. So she married Usamah ibn Zayd after that."
"27880","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah, that Abu Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughirah went out with Ali ibn Abi Talib to Yemen, and he sent to Fatimah bint Qays a divorce that remained of her divorce, and he assigned for her al-Harith ibn Hisham and Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah for maintenance. They said to her: By Allah, you have no maintenance unless you are pregnant. So she came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned to him their saying. He said: No, unless you are pregnant. And she sought his permission to move, so he permitted her. She said: Where do you see, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Ibn Umm Maktum, and he was blind; she lays aside her garments with him and he does not see her. When her waiting passed, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married her to Usamah ibn Zayd. Marwan sent to her Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb asking her about this hadith, so she narrated it to him. Marwan said: We have not heard this hadith except from a woman; we shall hold to the protection we found the people upon. Fatimah said when Marwan's saying reached her: Between me and you is the Qur'an. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: Do not expel them from their houses nor let them go out except that they commit a clear indecency, up to: Perhaps Allah will bring about after that a new matter. She said: This is for one who has return. What new matter is brought about after the third?"
"27881","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Amir narrated, from Fatimah bint Qays, that her husband divorced her three times, so she came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, complaining to him, and he granted her neither lodging nor maintenance. Umar ibn al-Khattab said: We do not abandon the Book of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and the Sunnah of His Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for the saying of a woman; perhaps she forgot. He said: Amir said: And she narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded her to observe her waiting in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum."
"27882","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri mentioned that Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb narrated to him that the daughter of Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl, and Fatimah bint Qays was her maternal aunt, and she was with Abdillah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, he divorced her three times, so her maternal aunt Fatimah bint Qays sent to her and moved her to her house, while Marwan ibn al-Hakam was over Madinah. Qabisah said: Marwan sent me to her and I asked her what prompted her to take a woman out of her house before her waiting ended. He said: She said: Because the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded me with that. He said: Then she recounted to me her hadith, then she said: And I dispute with you by the Book of Allah. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says in His Book: When you divorce women, divorce them for their waiting period, and count the waiting period, and fear Allah your Lord. Do not expel them from their houses nor let them go out except that they commit a clear indecency, up to: Perhaps Allah will bring about after that a new matter. Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: So when they reach their term the third time, retain them in kindness or release them in kindness. By Allah, Allah did not mention after the third any confinement, along with what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded me. He said: So I returned to Marwan and informed him of her news. He said: The hadith of a woman, the hadith of a woman. He said: Then he commanded concerning the woman, so she was returned to her house until her waiting ended."
"27883","Hushaym narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Fatimah bint Qays narrated to me that her husband divorced her irrevocably, so she disputed with him concerning lodging and maintenance to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. She said: So he granted neither lodging nor maintenance. And he said: O daughter of the family of Qays, lodging and maintenance are only upon one who has return to her."
"27884","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to us, he said: Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Fatimah bint Qays, that she informed him that she was under Abu Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughirah, and he divorced her the last of three divorces. She claimed that she came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and sought his ruling concerning leaving her house. So he commanded her to move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind man. Marwan refused to believe the hadith of Fatimah concerning the thrice-divorced woman leaving her house. And Urwah said: A'ishah denied that upon Fatimah bint Qays."
"27885","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Sayyar, Husayn, Mughirah, Ash'ath, Ibn Abi Khalid, and Dawud narrated to us, and Mujalid narrated it to us, and Isma'il, meaning Ibn Salim, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I entered upon Fatimah bint Qays and asked her about the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon her. She said: Her husband divorced her irrevocably. She said: So I disputed with him to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning lodging and maintenance. She said: So he granted me neither lodging nor maintenance, and he commanded me to observe my waiting in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum."
"27886","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Amir, from Fatimah bint Qays, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her concerning her waiting: Do not marry until you inform me."
"27887","Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Fatimah bint Qays narrated to me, she said: My husband divorced me three times, so I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he granted me neither lodging nor maintenance. And he said: Lodging and maintenance are only for one whose husband has return to her. And he commanded her to observe her waiting with Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind man."
"27888","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya narrated to us, from Amir, he said: Fatimah bint Qays narrated to me, she said: My husband divorced me three times, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded me to observe my waiting in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum."
"27889","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, meaning al-Sabi'i, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: My husband divorced me three times, so I wanted to move. So I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Move to the house of your cousin Amr Ibn Umm Maktum and observe your waiting with him."
"27890","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Fatimah bint Qays informed him that she was under Abu Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughirah, and he divorced her the last of three divorces. She claimed that she came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and sought his ruling concerning leaving her house. So he commanded her to move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind man. Marwan refused but to suspect the hadith of Fatimah concerning the divorced woman leaving her house. And Urwah claimed, he said: He said: So A'ishah denied that upon Fatimah."
"27891","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to us, from Amir, he said: I came to Madinah and I came to Fatimah bint Qays, and she narrated to me that her husband divorced her in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him on a detachment. His brother said to me: Go out of the house. I said: I have maintenance and lodging until the term ends. He said: No. She said: So I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I said: So-and-so divorced me, and his brother expelled me and denied me lodging and maintenance. So he sent to him and said: What is it with you and the daughter of the family of Qays? He said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother divorced her three times altogether. She said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Look, O daughter of the family of Qays, maintenance and lodging are for a woman upon her husband only as long as he has return to her. If he has no return to her, there is neither maintenance nor lodging. Go out and stay with so-and-so woman. Then he said: Men converse with her. Stay with Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is blind and does not see you. Then he said: Do not marry until I marry you. She said: A man of Quraysh proposed to me, so I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seeking his counsel. He said: Will you not marry one more beloved to me than him? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, marry me to whom you love. She said: So he married me to Usamah ibn Zayd. He said: When I wanted to go out, she said: Sit until I narrate to you a hadith from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out one day and prayed the midday prayer, then sat, and the people were startled. He said: Sit, O people, for I did not stand in this standing of mine from alarm, but Tamim al-Dari came to me and informed me a report that kept me from the midday rest, from joy and delight of the eye. I wished to spread to you the joy of your Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He informed me that a party of his cousins rode the sea, and a violent wind struck them, and the wind drove them to an island they did not know. They sat in the small boat of the ship until they went out to the island, and they found something hairy, abundantly hairy, not knowing whether it was a man or a woman. They greeted him and he returned their greeting. They said: Will you not inform us? He said: I shall neither inform you nor seek news from you, but this monastery which you have approached, in it is one most eager for your news to inform you and seek news from you. They said: We said: Who are you? She said: I am al-Jassasah. So they went until they came to the monastery, and they found a man bound, severely bound, showing grief, complaining much. They greeted him and he returned it to them. He said: Who are you? They said: From the Arabs. He said: What did the Arabs do, has their Prophet come forth yet? They said: Yes. He said: What did the Arabs do? They said: Good; they believed in him and affirmed him. He said: That is better for them. He had an enemy and Allah made him prevail over them. He said: The Arabs today, their god is one, their religion is one, and their word is one. They said: Yes. He said: What happened to the spring of Zughar? He said: They said: Sound; its people drink from it for their lips and water their crops from it. He said: What happened to the palms between Amman and Baysan? They said: Sound; its produce gives food every year. He said: What happened to the lake of Tabariyyah? They said: Full. He said: So he sighed, then sighed, then sighed, then he swore: If I were to come out of this place of mine, I would leave no land of Allah's earth but I would tread it, except Taybah; I have no authority over it. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: At this my joy ended, three times. Taybah is Madinah. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has forbidden al-Dajjal to enter it. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, swore: By Allah besides whom there is no god, it has no narrow nor wide road, in plain nor mountain, but upon it is an angel brandishing a sword until the Day of Resurrection. Al-Dajjal cannot enter it upon its people."
"27892","Amir said: So I met al-Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah and I narrated to him the hadith of Fatimah bint Qays. He said: I bear witness upon my father that he narrated to me as Fatimah narrated to you, except that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is toward the east."
"27893","He said: Then I met al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and I mentioned to him the hadith of Fatimah. He said: I bear witness upon A'ishah that she narrated to me as Fatimah narrated to you, except that she said: The two sanctuaries are forbidden to him: Makkah and Madinah."
"27894","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came one day hastening, ascended the minbar, and it was announced among the people: The congregational prayer. So the people gathered. He said: O people, I did not call you for a desired matter nor for fear, but Tamim al-Dari informed me that a group from Palestine rode the sea, and the wind cast them onto an island among the islands of the sea, and they found a shaggy beast, not known whether male or female from the abundance of its hair. They said: Who are you? It said: I am al-Jassasah. They said: Inform us. It said: I shall neither inform you nor seek news from you, but in this monastery is a man eager to inform you and to seek news from you. So they entered the monastery, and there was a one-eyed man bound in iron. He said: Who are you? They said: We are Arabs. He said: Has the Prophet been sent among you? They said: Yes. He said: Have the Arabs followed him? They said: Yes. He said: That is better for them. He said: What did Persia do, has it been conquered? They said: No. He said: But it will be conquered. Then he said: What happened to the spring of Zughar? They said: It is flowing, full. He said: What happened to the palms of Baysan, has it borne fruit? They said: Yes, its earliest. He said: So he leapt a leap until we thought he would escape. We said: Who are you? He said: I am al-Dajjal. Indeed I shall tread all the earth except Makkah and Taybah. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Rejoice, O assembly of Muslims, this is Taybah; it shall not be entered."
